{"assets":[],"contentKind":"statement","contestId":"24","diagnostics":[],"document":{"children":[{"attrs":{"level":1,"role":"title"},"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"D. Broken robot"}],"kind":"heading"},{"attrs":{"role":"time_limit"},"children":[{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"time limit per test"},{"kind":"text","text":":"}],"kind":"container"},{"kind":"text","text":"2 seconds"}],"kind":"container"},{"attrs":{"role":"memory_limit"},"children":[{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"memory limit per test"},{"kind":"text","text":":"}],"kind":"container"},{"kind":"text","text":"256 megabytes"}],"kind":"container"},{"attrs":{"role":"body"},"children":[{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"You received as a gift a very clever robot walking on a rectangular board. Unfortunately, you understood that it is broken and behaves rather strangely (randomly). The board consists of "},{"kind":"math_inline","text":"N"},{"kind":"text","text":" rows and "},{"kind":"math_inline","text":"M"},{"kind":"text","text":" columns of cells. The robot is initially at some cell on the "},{"kind":"math_inline","text":"i"},{"kind":"text","text":"-th row and the "},{"kind":"math_inline","text":"j"},{"kind":"text","text":"-th column. Then at every step the robot could go to some another cell. The aim is to go to the bottommost ("},{"kind":"math_inline","text":"N"},{"kind":"text","text":"-th) row. The robot can stay at it's current cell, move to the left, move to the right, or move to the cell below the current. If the robot is in the leftmost column it cannot move to the left, and if it is in the rightmost column it cannot move to the right. At every step all possible moves are equally probable. Return the expected number of step to reach the bottommost row."}],"kind":"paragraph"}],"kind":"section"},{"attrs":{"role":"input_specification"},"children":[{"attrs":{"level":2},"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"Input"}],"kind":"heading"},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"On the first line you will be 